    thinking: "**Considering Design Goals**\n\nI\'m now focusing on translating the design document\'s features into concrete web application elements. I\'m prioritizing the visual appeal, especially the floating header and immersive high-quality imagery. The goal is to build a sleek user experience.\n\n\n**Defining Core Functionality**\n\nI\'ve moved on to fleshing out the product presentation. I envision floating cards for the product families. Interactive modals or detail views will offer responsive information. I\'m focusing on \"Pourquoi choisir R\303\252ve Parfum\303\251,\" and the \"Trouver ma senteur\" section\'s scent quiz. I\'m also planning the full boutique catalog with robust search and product specification views for easy customer option selection. The user can create the custom WhatsApp template automatically! I\'m now conceptualizing \"Mariages & \303\211v\303\251nements\" as a detailed, tailored request form.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Set**\n\nI\'m now thinking about specific sections like \"R\303\251unions \303\240 domicile,\" which needs an intuitive booking tool that outputs a direct WhatsApp request. Also, I\'m conceptualizing the \"Avis clients\" page for reviews. I\'m prioritizing an elegant dark/cozy theme with specific color codes, typography, and motion animations. Full-screen responsiveness and a persistent floating WhatsApp icon or sticky bar for mobile are key. I\'m also planning out clear explanations for \"Livraison & Pr\303\251commande.\"\nI\'m designing a modular application and declaring files: `/src/types.ts` for product definitions and `/src/data.ts` for the product item collection.\n\n\n**Detailing Core Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the component breakdown. I\'m focusing on truly rich product representations, not placeholders. I\'m building a floating header with a capsule-like design and elegant menu. I\'m imagining an interactive scent quiz with beautiful animated radio buttons. I\'m also planning floating, rounded product cards, and a review section that promotes direct WhatsApp submission. Finally, I\'m working out the state navigation for a clean and seamless user flow across all key pages.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now set up the typography fonts (Cormorant Garamond, Inter, and JetBrains Mono) and configure Tailwind CSS theme variables inside `/src/index.css` to create a luxurious and cozy visual style."
