    thinking: "**Initiating Component Creation**\n\nI\'m now starting on the ScentQuiz.tsx component, aiming to bring the \"Trouver ma senteur\" section to life. I\'ve begun outlining the questions; the first one will be \"Is this for you or a gift?\". I\'ll need to define the logic for option A\'s responses, and work through all the options.\n\n\n**Defining Quiz Options**\n\nI\'ve moved on to fleshing out the scent quiz options. I\'m setting up the second question on olfactory ambiance, mapping each option to our declared scent families. I\'m also preparing the questions on room usage and preferred diffusion type, and their associated choices. It\'s becoming clearer how the quiz will flow.\n\n\n**Refining Product Recommendations**\n\nI\'m now integrating logic for product recommendations based on quiz answers. I\'m focusing on calculating a compatibility score based on scent family matches between answers and product attributes, and then pre-selecting two targeted products from the `PRODUCTS` list that fit the preference. For instance, based on intense diffusion preferences, I will recommend specific products like \"Sachet de Fondants Coeur Fleur\". I\'m aiming for a seamless user experience, with clearly recommended products at the quiz\'s conclusion, and a clear call to action!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now build the Scent Wizard `/src/components/ScentQuiz.tsx` module. This implements the quiz requested in section 5: an interactive, smooth 4-step wizard with beautiful state feedback, custom recommendations, and automated WhatsApp text generation based on the matching olfactory families."
