    thinking: "**Defining Premium Section**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into `App.tsx`, starting around line 111. My goal is to revamp the Accueil Section to be exclusively premium, perfectly aligning with the given prompts. I\'m focusing on key replacements and improvements. First up, I\'m specifying a badge for the Atelier-Hero component.\n\n\n**Refining Premium Messaging**\n\nI\'ve just refined the title for the artisan creations. It now reads: \"Des cr\303\251ations parfum\303\251es naturelles, <span className=\\\"text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-pink via-brand-purple to-brand-wax font-light italic\\\">faites main</span> avec <span className=\\\"font-light italic text-brand-pink\\\">douceur</span>\". Next, I am updating the primary button CTA, and formulating the micro-reassurance cards. I\'m aiming for four cards that instill confidence: soy wax, Grasse perfumes, pre-order in two weeks, and customizable options. I\'ll include the category images next.\n\n\n**Listing Premium Creations**\n\nI am now structuring the premium content with four distinct product entries: Decorative compositions and scented, wax melts, candles, and scented frames. Each will feature an image, a description, and a \"Pre-order\" badge. I\'m building clickable buttons that direct to their respective category in the boutique.\n\n\n**Formulating R\303\252ve Parfum\303\251 Section**\n\nI\'m structuring the \"Pourquoi choisir R\303\252ve Parfum\303\251 ?\" section, formulating the title and arguments. I\'m focusing on the image and button and four concise arguments: natural ingredients, handmade craftsmanship, personalization options, and suitability as a gift. Next, I\'ll start formulating the Senteur guide section.\n\n\n**Structuring Senteur Guide**\n\nI\'m now structuring the Senteur Guide section with its associated CTA. The CTA is \"Lancer le guide senteur\", which activates the quiz modal and scrolls the user down the page. I\'m focusing on providing users with fragrance recommendations, in categories such as floral, fruity, gourmand, fresh, soft, or warm. The goal is a user-friendly guide.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Adding Event Section**\n\nI\'m developing a new, concise \"Section \303\251v\303\251nements.\" It\'ll introduce services for weddings, corporate gifts, and business committees. The left side includes the title, \"Mariages, \303\251v\303\251nements & comit\303\251s d\342\200\231entreprise,\" a description of personalized creations with volume-based discounts, and a \"Demander un devis\" CTA. On the right, I\'m integrating three overlapping mini-cards that describe wedding favors, guest gifts, and corporate gift sets. I am using elegant thumbnails and concise text for each.\n\n\n**Integrating Client Reviews**\n\nI\'m now integrating client testimonials to build social proof. I\'m showcasing feedback like \"Une odeur douce qui reste longtemps\" from Sophie Dumont and others to bolster the brand\'s credibility. I\'m including a mention stating \"Avis issus de retours clients Facebook / Messenger.\" A CTA button \"Voir les avis clients\" will lead to a specific page. Finally, a new CTA block is coming up.\n\n\n**Implementing Fragrance Filters**\n\nI\'m now integrating fragrance filters into the boutique experience. These will include olfactory families, occasions, price range sliders, customizability options, and delivery/pickup preferences. The goal is to build a sleek sliding menu for a high-end feel. I\'ll define these filter states within `App.tsx` for easy access. I\'m currently assessing existing state variables, specifically around lines 41-60.\n\n\n**Adding Boutique Filters**\n\nI\'m expanding the boutique\'s filtering capabilities. I\'ve introduced `maxPrice`, `onlyCustomizable`, `occasionFilter`, and `deliveryRetraitFilter` state variables. I am updating the filter logic to incorporate these new criteria, focusing on building an interactive and responsive user experience. I\'m focusing on lines 41-60 to be able to fully implement the changes and refine the experience.\n\n\n**Refining Filter Logic**\n\nI\'m refining the filtering logic to precisely match product attributes with user selections. I\'m focusing on lines 41-60 in `App.tsx` and am refining the scent filter by assessing whether the scent belongs to a filtered family. The occasion filters are getting better, now matching occasion values such as \'Cadeau,\' \'Maison,\' \'Mariage,\' and \'Voiture\' to product categories and customizability.\n\n\n"
