  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Current Status**\n\nI\'ve determined that the `ReviewSection` component currently populates the \'avis\' tab, but I\'m thinking beyond this. The prompt calls for a dedicated page for Reviews, Inspirations, and Proof, which will require specialized blocks and visual elements, such as screen captures. I\'m focusing on how to integrate the existing section into the new page.\n\n\n**Designing New Page Layout**\n\nI\'m now designing the layout for the `/avis-clients` route, ensuring a professional aesthetic. The structure will include a hero section with cards and bubbles, a grid of six reviews sourced from different platforms (I\'ll leverage existing mock data), a special block for \"Senteur durable\" with a custom button, and finally, a grid of screen captures or styled review cards for social proof. I\'ll make sure to style those appropriately and label them.\n\n\n**Developing Delivery Features**\n\nI\'m now focused on the `/livraison` section, aiming for an animated and feature-rich system. I\'m structuring it precisely as requested: a hero section with a \"Pr\303\251commande & retrait\" badge and a WhatsApp CTA, a pre-order block detailing the process, a delivery timeline, shipping periods with a responsive layout, and a section for transport providers. I\'ve confirmed that `App.tsx` already has a `currentTab === \'livraison\'` block, which I\'ll build upon.\n\n\n**Refining Review Presentation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"AVIS CLIENTS\" section, specifically how to display the reviews effectively. I\'m leaning toward creating a dedicated, beautifully animated reviews page within `ReviewSection.tsx`. I\'ve re-read the prompt and the layout must feature a hero with a \"Retours clients\" badge, a six-review grid, a dedicated \"senteur durable\" block, and a grid for screen captures. I\'m planning to style those captures as elegant cards to simulate premium social proof.\n\n\n**Implementing Final Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now implementing the final enhancements for `/src/components/ReviewSection.tsx`, focusing on replacing emojis with Lucide icons for a professional look. I\'ve confirmed `motion/react` imports. I\'ve outlined the necessary changes and have begun writing the component, aiming for a modern, fully animated presentation. I will integrate the \"Laisser un avis\" section and final CTA.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I am going to rewrite `/src/components/ReviewSection.tsx` to build a highly premium, modern, and immersive **Avis Clients** (Customer Reviews) page. This implementation follows all requirements:\n1. **Strictly 0 emojis** replaced by professional, beautiful Lucide icons (`Sparkles`, `Star`, `Facebook`, `Heart`, `Award`, etc.).\n2. **Beautiful Hero** with an interactive layout.\n3. **An elegant grid of custom testimonials** showing different products, dates, and ratings.\n4. **Interactive screens replica and screen-captures area** with high-fidelity styled review bubble mockups (to maintain private names while showcasing beautiful social proof).\n5. **Special \"Senteur Durable\" focus block** with a call-to-action button to help them find their perfect fragrance.\n6. **\"Laisser un avis\" double CTA section** for Facebook and Google Business with sophisticated feedback and tooltips.\n7. **Final boutique call-to-action**.\n8. **Premium micro-animations** using `motion/react`."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 880819822
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
