    thinking: "**Analyzing the component structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the component structure within `LegalPages.tsx`. My current focus is implementing the individual components: `LegalPageLayout`, `LegalHero`, and `LegalSection`. I want to ensure each fulfills its role in the design.\n\n\n**Restructuring Component Order**\n\nI\'m now restructuring the component order within `LegalPages.tsx`, incorporating `LegalInfoList` and a `Footer`, either a global one or a sub-footer as per prompt. I\'m focusing on aligning with the \"PAGE \303\200 CONSTRUIRE : MENTIONS L\303\211GALES\" guidelines, ensuring exact component inclusion: `LegalPageLayout`, `LegalHero`, `LegalSection`, `LegalInfoList`, and `Footer` or Contact link. Placeholders \"[\303\200 compl\303\251ter]\" will replace the generic text. I\'ll maintain cohesion and full sub-tab integration.\n\n\n**Defining Legal Component Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the specifics for each legal component, starting with the `LegalHero`. I\'ve outlined its title and under-text content. I\'m moving on to populate the \'\303\211diteur du site\' section including names, status, and contact details, marking placeholders \"[\303\200 compl\303\251ter]\" for missing data like SIRET numbers and addresses. I\'m also preparing for the \'Responsable de publication\' and \'H\303\251bergeur\' sections, filling in the generic placeholders, and defining the \'Propri\303\251t\303\251 intellectuelle\' and \'Responsabilit\303\251\' contents.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I am now replacing `/src/components/LegalPages.tsx` with a highly polished legal layout. It is custom-tailored to avoid any \"generic storefront\" look:\n1. **LegalHero**: Promotes a clean, professional, non-commercial tone with the exact specified subtitle.\n2. **Sub-components Partitioning**: Organizes sections neatly using modular, readable constructs:\n   - `LegalSection`: Declares individual panels styled with thin separators (`--border`).\n   - `LegalInfoList`: Lists contact values, micro-enterprise details, SIRET lines with explicit `[\303\200 compl\303\251ter]` placeholders as requested.\n   - `LegalPageLayout`: Wraps the layout cleanly at a `max-w-[900px]` width constraint.\n3. **Exact French Copy**: Formulates precise statements for the Publisher, Editor, Publisher Officer, Host, Intellectual Property Protection, and Pre-order / Delivery Confirmation checks.\n4. **Transition Trigger**: Links the final CTA back to the contact route dynamically via `onNavigateToContact`.\n\nLet\'s use `create_file` with the `Overwrite: true` argument."
