    thinking: "**Cleaning Up Emojis!**\n\nI\'m focused on removing lingering emojis. The `DeliveryPage.tsx` file has one on line 390. I\'m also going to check `src/App.tsx`, and `LegalPages.tsx`, for any additional occurrences, so I can conduct a thorough clean-up of the emoji clutter. Afterward, I need to see what\'s in `src/components/AboutPage`.\n\n\n**Identifying Emoji Instances**\n\nI\'ve got a list of emojis that require replacement. In `DeliveryPage.tsx`, I\'ll swap the `\360\237\217\241` emoji on line 390 for either a `Home` icon or `Sparkles` from `lucide-react`. Then, I\'ll revise the `\360\237\215\202` emoji on line 692 of `src/App.tsx`, and I\'ll also change `\342\217\263 Pr\303\251commande` on lines 288, 317, 345, and 375 to `<Clock className=\"w-3 h-3 text-brand-pink shrink-0\" /> Pr\303\251commande`. Lastly, I will swap the `\360\237\244\235` emoji on line 176 of `LegalPages.tsx`.\n\n\n**Expanding Emoji Hunt**\n\nI\'m now expanding the search beyond the initially identified files. I need to check `AboutPage.tsx`, `ContactPage.tsx`, `CustomizationPage.tsx`, `EventQuoteBuilder.tsx`, `HomePartiesBuilder.tsx`, `ReviewSection.tsx`, and `ScentQuiz.tsx`. My plan is to use `grep` to recursively search for specific emojis like `\360\237\244\235`, `\360\237\223\270`, `\360\237\222\254`, `\360\237\244\215`, `\360\237\216\201`, `\342\234\250`, and `\360\237\214\270` within the `src/components/` directory. I\'m also planning to inspect the accueil/home page and add some brand-improving features as I edit.\n\n\n**Designing Home Page Upgrade**\n\nI\'m now formulating a plan for the home page upgrade, focusing on a premium design. I\'m prioritizing the home (accueil) page. I\'ve broken down the design into clear bullet points: First, I\'ll systematically remove low-quality emojis, replacing them with custom Lucide icons in glassmorphic elements. Second, I plan to introduce a highly interactive \"Mood & Olfactory Wheel\" component on the home page, which dynamically showcases signature scents based on user interaction.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Animation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"Aromatic Fall\" visual particles using Framer Motion. I\'m focusing on crafting a slow-drifting flower petal animation for the Hero and Section views. This is an upgrade to the accueil page. I\'ve confirmed that the image-generation skill isn\'t required, and I\'m transitioning back to cleaning up emojis in other pages. Let\'s first search those pages!\n\n\n"
