e array of mood objects. I am using the provided data structure, with each object now representing a mood, including its ID, label, description, and related scents. I\'m carefully organizing the `color` property as well. I am working on the mapping logic to render the mood buttons dynamically. I will define how each mood button will dynamically adjust on active state.\n\n\n**Styling Mood Button States**\n\nI\'m now implementing the visual states for the mood buttons, focusing on active and hover states. I\'m leveraging Tailwind classes to achieve the desired effects. For the active state, I\'m applying a distinct background color and border, enhancing visual feedback. The hover state features a subtle border change and background opacity adjustment for a smooth user experience. The color of the button changes based on its state.\n\n\n\n**Refining Scent Recommendations**\n\nI am now updating the scent recommendations based on the active mood. I\'m focusing on the logic to dynamically display scent suggestions. I\'ve integrated conditional rendering, adjusting the content displayed within the `div` based on the `activeMood` state. The content is now rendering correctly. I am now focusing on the visual styling.\n\n\n**Implementing Scent Filtering**\n\nI\'m now implementing scent filtering based on the active mood within the component. My focus is on dynamically displaying products based on the user\'s selected mood. I\'m currently working on correctly applying the `filter` function to the `PRODUCTS` array to ensure relevant scents are displayed. I need to make sure the logic is returning the correct products for each mood, and I need to style it next.\n\n\n**Styling Product Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on styling the product display within the mood wheel, making sure the user experience is visually consistent. I am now applying Tailwind classes to each product card, using `flex`, `items-center`, `gap-4`, and adjusting the text alignment. I am also adjusting the image dimensions and adding borders. I will style the button, by updating hover states for seamless interaction.\n\n\n\n**Adding Hero Visual Element**\n\nI\'m now integrating the floating particle canvas within the Hero section\'s background. I\'m focusing on positioning the element absolutely and managing overflow. I\'m adding a motion div with initial and animate states, creating the animation of aromatic petals or leaves. The particle effect creates an intriguing background for the user\'s experience.\n\n\n"
