  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Color Palette Variables**\n\nI\'ve defined the initial color variables. These include a deep, dark brand background (`--color-brand-bg`), a slightly lighter depth variant (`--color-brand-depth`), a beautiful soft pink (`--color-brand-pink`), and a purple shade (`--color-brand-purple`). I am now considering how these will translate to visual outputs.\n\n\n**Expanding Color Palette Details**\n\nI\'m adding new colors: `--color-brand-cream` (a soft cream-white), `--color-brand-wax` (a warm beige), and `--color-brand-text-muted` (a muted gray). I am also working on using these new colors with white to add contrast and highlight details. White will be used for premium badges, card accents, and highlighting blocks for a touch of elegance and clarity.\n\n\n**Designing Visual Displays**\n\nI am now focusing on high-contrast, light-white layouts for inspiration grids and headers. I\'m also planning clean, modern carousels or boards. These will display \"mises en situation\" for weddings, home decor, seasonal content, and atelier life, using carefully curated imagery to showcase each category\'s lifestyle context. I am building a brand new component `/src/components`.\n\n\n**Crafting a New Carousel**\n\nI\'m deep in the design of the `LifestyleCarousel.tsx` component. I\'m focusing on a beautiful, interactive, swipeable carousel with animated effects from `motion/react`. I will ensure that it supports high-quality Unsplash images, elegant captions for \"mises en situation,\" and actionable navigation targets for customization and booking. I will also incorporate white highlights for contrast with the dark background. The first two examples that will be displayed are \"Mariage Romantique\" and \"Atelier Cocooning\".\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 23
      nanos: 985975054
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
